    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30669" root="عن" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَانٌّ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَانَّةٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَنَانٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And for the former,
see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَنُونٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also, the former, <i>A long mountain</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَبَل</span>), (K, TA, in some copies of the K
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَبْل</span> [i. e. <i>rope</i>],) <i>that presents itself in the direction in which one is going, and interrupts his way.</i>
(TA.)

